<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(Energy Availability)/Pg 15 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

237 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(Your body relies on readily available fuel to perform well during exercise. Eating appropriately before a workout helps ensure your muscles and brain have access to energy, supporting strength, focus, and endurance. When nutrition timing is off, workouts can feel harder, less effective, and more fatiguing than they need to be.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

238 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 66 0 R/Pg 15 0 R/A[781 0 R 0]/K[9]>>
endobj

239 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(Muscle Recovery & repair)/Pg 15 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

240 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(Exercise creates small amounts of muscle stress that require proper nutrition to recover from. Post-workout meals or snacks provide the building blocks your body needs to repair muscle tissue and adapt to training. Consistent recovery nutrition can help reduce soreness, support muscle maintenance, and improve long-term training results.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

241 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 66 0 R/Pg 15 0 R/A[782 0 R 0]/K[12]>>
endobj

242 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(Blood Sugar Balance & Performance)/Pg 15 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

243 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 66 0 R/E(The timing of your meals influences how stable your blood sugar remains before, during, and after exercise. Balanced nutrition around workouts helps prevent sharp energy spikes and crashes that can affect performance and mood. Stable blood sugar supports more consistent workouts, better recovery, and steadier energy throughout the day.)/Pg 15 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

244 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 66 0 R/Pg 15 0 R/A[783 0 R 0]/K[15]>>
endobj

245 0 obj
