endobj

313 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(Before a workout, your body needs accessible energy to support movement, focus, and endurance. Pre-workout nutrition helps prepare your muscles and nervous system while reducing early fatigue. The goal isn\220t a large meal, but enough fuel to train comfortably and effectively.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

314 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(Carbohydrates, protein & fats \204 what matters most)/Pg 18 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

315 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(Carbohydrates are the main fuel source for most workouts and support performance and intensity. Protein helps protect muscle tissue, especially during longer or more demanding sessions. Fats play a smaller role before exercise and are best kept moderate, as they digest more slowly.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

316 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(Hydration basics)/Pg 18 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

317 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 69 0 R/E(Hydration supports circulation, temperature control, and overall workout performance. Even mild dehydration can affect energy and focus, making training feel harder. Consistent fluid intake throughout the day works better than trying to hydrate all at once before exercise.)/Pg 18 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

