328 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 70 0 R/E(Choose light, easy-to-digest foods that provide quick energy without feeling heavy. Simple carbohydrates paired with a small amount of protein can help support energy and focus while minimizing digestive discomfort.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

329 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 70 0 R/E(1\2052 hours before training)/Pg 19 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

330 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 70 0 R/E(A balanced meal works best when you have more time before exercise. Aim for carbohydrates for fuel, protein for muscle support, and a moderate amount of fat to help keep you satisfied without slowing digestion.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

