<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 70 0 R/E(Early-morning / fasted workouts)/Pg 19 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

332 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 70 0 R/E(Some people prefer to train with little or no food first thing in the morning. If energy feels low, a small snack or liquid option before training can help support performance without feeling too heavy.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

333 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 70 0 R/E(Low-appetite options)/Pg 19 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

334 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 70 0 R/E(When hunger is low, smaller portions or liquid foods can be easier to tolerate and digest. Smoothies, yogurt, fruit, or simple snacks can provide enough fuel to support your workout without feeling heavy or overwhelming.)/Pg 19 0 R/K[12]>>
