366 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 72 0 R/E(Recovery window explained)/Pg 21 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

367 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 72 0 R/E(The idea of a strict \215post-workout window\216 is often overstated. While eating after training supports recovery, it doesn\220t need to happen immediately or within a narrow timeframe. What matters most is consistently meeting your overall nutrition needs throughout the day.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

368 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 72 0 R/E(Protein needs for muscle repair)/Pg 21 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

369 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 72 0 R/E(Protein provides the building blocks needed to repair and maintain muscle after exercise. Including protein in a post-workout meal or snack supports recovery and training adaptations over time.  Consistent protein intake throughout the day matters more than perfect timing.)/Pg 21 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

370 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 72 0 R/E(YOUR )/Pg 21 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

