386 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 73 0 R/E(If you\220re hungry right after exercise, a light snack with protein and carbohydrates can support early recovery and muscle repair. This approach can be especially helpful after longer or more intense workouts, but it\220s not essential if a balanced meal is planned soon afterward.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

387 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 73 0 R/E(Within 1\2052 hours post-workout)/Pg 22 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

388 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 73 0 R/E(A balanced meal within this timeframe supports muscle repair, energy replenishment, and overall recovery. Including protein, carbohydrates, and fluids helps restore what was used during training and prepares your body for your next workout or daily activities.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

389 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 73 0 R/E(When you don\220t feel hungry)/Pg 22 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

390 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 73 0 R/E(Appetite can be low after exercise, particularly following high-intensity or demanding sessions. In these situations, smaller portions or liquid options can make recovery nutrition easier and more comfortable. Focus on gentle nourishment and eat a full meal once hunger returns naturally.)/Pg 22 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

