<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 76 0 R/E(Pre & Post Workout Nutrition Guide | 16 )/Pg 25 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

456 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 76 0 R/E(Digestion plays an important role in workout comfort. Heavy, greasy, or highly processed foods can sometimes feel uncomfortable when eaten too close to exercise. Choosing simpler, minimally processed foods before training can help reduce bloating, cramping, or sluggishness during movement.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

457 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 76 0 R/E(After workouts, digestion may still be settling, especially after intense sessions. Gentle, familiar foods can help support recovery without overwhelming your system. Paying attention to how different foods make you feel can help you refine your personal pre- and post-workout routine over time.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

458 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 76 0 R/E(Digestion Tip)/Pg 25 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

459 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 76 0 R/E(Eating simpler foods closer to workouts and saving heavier meals for later can improve comfort and performance.)/Pg 25 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

