468 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(Training Under-Fueled)/Pg 26 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

469 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(Going into workouts without enough fuel can lead to low energy, dizziness, poor performance, and slower progress over time. When the body doesn\220t have adequate carbohydrates or overall energy, it may rely more heavily on stress hormones, making workouts feel harder and recovery less effective overall. Even small, balanced pre-workout snacks can support better focus, endurance, and strength during training.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

470 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(Skipping Recovery Nutrition)/Pg 26 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

471 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(After exercise, the body needs nutrients to repair muscles, replenish energy, and support recovery. Skipping post-workout nutrition may increase soreness, delay recovery, and affect future workouts. A combination of protein and carbohydrates helps the body adapt to exercise and supports long-term consistency.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

472 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(Remember, fueling your body doesn\220t need to be complicated. Small, consistent choices before and after workouts can make a meaningful difference in energy, performance, and recovery. Focus on progress over perfection and build habits that feel sustainable for your lifestyle.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

473 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 77 0 R/T(COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID)/E(COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID)/Pg 26 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

474 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(Over-Reliance on Supplements)/Pg 26 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

475 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(Supplements are often marketed as essential for fitness performance and recovery, but they are not a replacement for real, nourishing food. Over-reliance on powders or pills can lead to nutrient gaps, unnecessary expense, and missed benefits of whole foods. Whole foods provide vitamins, minerals, fiber, and phytonutrients that supplements can\220t fully replace. Supplements should support a balanced, not replace it.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[11]>>
endobj

476 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(Ignoring Hydration Needs)/Pg 26 0 R/K[12]>>
endobj

477 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 77 0 R/E(Focusing only on food while neglecting hydration can significantly impact workout performance and recovery. Even mild dehydration may reduce strength, endurance, and concentration. Fluids help regulate body temperature, support circulation, and aid nutrient transport to muscles.)/Pg 26 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

