<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 78 0 R/T(Weight Loss Goals)/E(Weight Loss Goals)/Pg 27 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

486 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 78 0 R/E(When weight loss is a goal, pre- and post-workout nutrition should still support energy and recovery. Skipping fuel entirely can lead to low energy, poor workout performance, or increased hunger later in the day. Balanced meals and snacks that include protein and fiber-rich foods can help support training while promoting steady appetite and consistency.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

487 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 78 0 R/T(Muscle Building Goals)/E(Muscle Building Goals)/Pg 27 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

488 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 78 0 R/E(Supporting muscle growth requires consistent nourishment around training. Pre-workout foods can help support workout intensity, while post-workout meals support muscle repair and adaptation. Prioritizing regular meals with adequate protein and carbohydrates helps your body respond positively to strength training over time.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

489 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 78 0 R/T(Blood Sugar Balance & Energy Crashes)/E(Blood Sugar Balance & Energy Crashes)/Pg 27 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

490 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 78 0 R/E(Large gaps between meals or highly refined foods can sometimes lead to energy highs and lows around workouts. Choosing balanced meals and snacks with a mix of carbohydrates, protein, and fats can help support steadier energy levels. Paying attention to timing and food quality may reduce post-workout fatigue or energy crashes.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

491 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 78 0 R/T(Digestive Sensitivity)/E(Digestive Sensitivity)/Pg 27 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

492 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 78 0 R/E(Some people experience digestive discomfort around exercise, especially with heavy or unfamiliar foods. Opting for simpler, easy-to-digest options before workouts and gentler recovery foods afterward can help improve comfort. Listening to your body and adjusting food choices based on tolerance is key.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

493 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/Figure/P 78 0 R/Pg 27 0 R/A[853 0 R 0]/K[8]>>
endobj

494 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/P 78 0 R/T(SPECIAL CONSIDERATIONS)/E(SPECIAL CONSIDERATIONS)/Pg 27 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

495 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 78 0 R/E(Everyone\220s body responds differently to food and exercise. These considerations can help you adjust pre- and post-workout nutrition in a way that feels supportive, comfortable, and sustainable based on your individual needs.)/Pg 27 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

