567 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(These are often marketed for faster recovery, but balanced meals and fluids usually provide what the body needs after training.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[13]>>
endobj

568 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(Nutrition around workouts works best when it starts with real food. Meals and snacks provide the energy and nourishment needed for training and recovery, while supplements remain optional rather than essential.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[14]>>
endobj

569 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 81 0 R/E(For most people, consistent meals, balanced food choices, and hydration do more to support energy and recovery than any supplement.)/Pg 30 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

