580 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(COMMON QUESTIONS & REASSURING ANSWERS)/Pg 31 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

581 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(Questions around eating before and after workouts are very common. Nutrition advice can feel confusing or contradictory, especially when routines, schedules, and appetite change from day to day. These answers are meant to offer clarity and reassurance\204there is flexibility, and small adjustments often work better than strict rules.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

582 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 82 0 R/T(Do I Need to Eat Before Every Workout?)/E(Do I Need to Eat Before Every Workout?)/Pg 31 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

583 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(No, eating before every workout isn\220t required. Some people feel better with food before training, while others feel comfortable exercising with little or no food, especially for lighter or shorter sessions.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

584 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(The goal is to support your energy and comfort. If you notice low energy, dizziness, or poor focus during workouts, adding a small snack beforehand may help. If you feel fine without eating, that can also be okay.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

585 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 82 0 R/T(Is It Okay to Work Out Without Eating First?)/E(Is It Okay to Work Out Without Eating First?)/Pg 31 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

586 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(Yes, for some people and some types of workouts, training without eating first can feel completely comfortable. This is more common with low-intensity movement or shorter sessions.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

587 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(If workouts feel harder than expected or recovery feels slower, it may be helpful to experiment with a light snack or liquid option beforehand. Pay attention to how your body responds rather than following a fixed rule.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

588 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 82 0 R/T(Do Short Workouts Need Special Fueling?)/E(Do Short Workouts Need Special Fueling?)/Pg 31 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

589 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(Short workouts usually don\220t require anything special. If you\220re moving for a brief period and feel energized, your regular meals may already be enough.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

590 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(However, if short workouts still feel draining or are part of a busy day with long gaps between meals, a small snack before or after can help support energy and recovery. Simplicity works well here.)/Pg 31 0 R/K[10]>>
endobj

591 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 82 0 R/E(YOUR )/Pg 31 0 R/K[11]>>
