599 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 83 0 R/T(What If I Train Late in the Evening?)/E(What If I Train Late in the Evening?)/Pg 32 0 R/K[0]>>
endobj

600 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Evening workouts don\220t require a different approach, but timing can feel trickier. A balanced meal earlier in the evening often supports training better than exercising on an empty stomach.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

601 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(After late workouts, choose something nourishing but comfortable rather than heavy or overly large. Light meals or snacks can still support recovery without interfering with rest or sleep.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

602 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 83 0 R/T(What If I Miss My Post-Workout Meal?)/E(What If I Miss My Post-Workout Meal?)/Pg 32 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

603 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Missing a post-workout meal once in a while is not a problem. Recovery doesn\220t depend on a single meal or perfect timing.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

604 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(What matters more is overall nourishment across the day. Eating a balanced meal later on still supports recovery, even if it\220s not immediately after training.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

605 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H3/P 83 0 R/T(What If My Appetite Changes After Exercise?)/E(What If My Appetite Changes After Exercise?)/Pg 32 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

606 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(Appetite can vary after workouts\204sometimes hunger increases, other times it decreases. Both responses are normal.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

607 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(If appetite is low, smaller portions or liquid options can be easier. If hunger is higher, a more substantial meal may feel supportive. Let appetite guide portion size rather than forcing food at a specific time.)/Pg 32 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

608 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 83 0 R/E(YOUR )/Pg 32 0 R/K[9]>>
endobj

