endobj

617 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(Long-term results come from small, repeatable habits rather than perfect execution. Pre- and post-workout nutrition should feel supportive, flexible, and easy to maintain alongside your routine.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[1]>>
endobj

618 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(Focus on simple food choices you can repeat regularly without stress. Keeping meals and snacks familiar makes it easier to stay consistent over time. Planning ahead when possible and allowing flexibility when needed helps nutrition fit into real life rather than feeling like a rulebook.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[2]>>
endobj

619 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 84 0 R/E(Your appetite and energy levels can vary from day to day based on training, sleep, and stress. Paying attention to how your body feels before and after workouts helps guide food choices more effectively than strict timing or expectations. Eating when you\220re hungry and adjusting portions based on energy needs supports a healthier, more intuitive approach to fueling.)/Pg 33 0 R/K[3]>>
endobj

